  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Wyoming received $616M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, delivered through 2,662 awards with an average award size of $231K. Obligations are up 24.0% year over year. The Department of the Interior is the largest buyer in the state with $331M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $90.4M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $85.2M. Construction and infrastructure industries dominate spending: Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction accounts for $247M, Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $88.9M, and Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction accounts for $65.4M. RECORD STEEL AND CONSTRUCTION, INC. and G.S.E. CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INC. are the top two vendors with $130M and $109M respectively. Other significant vendors include THE ARMORED GROUP LLC with $26.4M and BRIDGER RICHARD JV LLC with $25.7M. Past fiscal-year obligations show growth from $390M in FY21 to $616M in FY26, with intermediate totals of $559M, $470M, $532M, and $497M for FY22 through FY25 respectively.",
    "sections": [
